Subject: Earthbend abilities: cast the permanents in hand before sinking mana into Ba Sing Se
Why: EarthbendAi.canPlay said yes whenever the AI controlled a land, so Ba Sing Se's
  {2}{G},{T}: Earthbend 2 was activated in the first main phase of every turn. Permanent spells
  wait for the second main phase (ComputerUtil.castPermanentInMain1), and by then the mana was
  gone: in the patched round robin Mono-Green Landfall activated it 4.35 times a game when it
  had Ba Sing Se, cast Mossborn Hydra in 31% of those games against 76% without the land, and
  won 44.2% against 58.2%. Now an activated earthbend with a mana cost is put off while a
  permanent card in hand could be paid for with the same mana.
Measured: `mtgsim gauntlet decks/standard/meta/mono-green-landfall.txt --vs <the other ten meta decks>
  -n 100 --seed 1`, default AI, Forge 7db198d72e, on 14 Nov 2026. With patches 0001-0010:
  47.4% (95% CI 44-50%, 474-526). With this patch added: 67.7% (65-71%, 677-323). Difference
  +20.3 points, 95% CI +16.0 to +24.5 (paired over the same 1,000 seeds: +17.7 to +22.9;
  209 losses became wins, 6 wins became losses). Games in which a card was cast, of 1,000:
  Mossborn Hydra 340 to 502, Icetill Explorer 295 to 534, Earthbender Ascension 298 to 451.
  Mirror with the patch (`match mono-green-landfall mono-green-landfall -n 200 --seed 1`):
  54.8% (48-62%).

